                        "glosses": [
                            "catenary; like a chain"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1c364dcc-730d-49d6-a841-5f5935eb1416",
                                "sense_id": "6b113c4f-961e-358f-9b69-a2fecbafc834",
                                "text": "At each joint of the three tiers of the catenarian chains respectively, one of the saddle pieces of cast-iron, formerly alluded to, are introduced."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4bb1c6a8-954e-3948-bb06-d8f1e81a1ace",
                        "entry_id": "d2e73393-8663-3eea-a269-98e2fa484bcd",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Shaped like a catenary; following the curve made by a chain or rope when suspended from both ends."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e9bce71d-b623-48ad-b562-70f688f343ee",
                                "sense_id": "4bb1c6a8-954e-3948-bb06-d8f1e81a1ace",
                                "text": "The curve so formed is a catenarian curve, and, when inverted, delineates the curve of a type of arch better able to resist forces of destruction than the earlier semicircular arch. Investigators who followed Galilei and studied the catenarian arch mathematically were able to show that a simple catenarian outline was formed by the chan suspeneded as already described, the length of the chain depending upon the required span and rise of the arch."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ab8a7aff-70bd-4df1-a015-13dd353b7c3d",
                                "sense_id": "4bb1c6a8-954e-3948-bb06-d8f1e81a1ace",
                                "text": "a catenarian curve/arch"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "bbe01122-25be-34e4-ab2c-0a3c22cf9b98",
                        "entry_id": "d2e73393-8663-3eea-a269-98e2fa484bcd",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Having the property that every ascending chain of prime ideals eventually stabilizes, meaning that there is a finite length for the chains of prime ideals."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "11ec3a81-0b65-445d-8d2d-a938d8a1c0cd",
                                "sense_id": "bbe01122-25be-34e4-ab2c-0a3c22cf9b98",
                                "text": "Each universally catenarian domain is catenarian and, hence, LFD."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
